## ✅ Acceptance Criteria

### Functionality
- [ ] Fetches CIA CSV from GitHub raw URL
- [ ] Implements 1-hour LocalStorage caching (monitoring frequency)
- [ ] Renders 6 visualizations (timeline, distribution, donut, heatmap, bar, feed)
- [ ] Displays alert banner for CRITICAL/HIGH anomalies in last 2 quarters
- [ ] Filters work correctly (severity, type, direction, year)
- [ ] Recent anomalies feed shows last 5 anomalies
- [ ] Tooltips show detailed Z-scores and metrics

### Data Accuracy
- [ ] Correctly identifies 12 anomalies out of 32 quarters (37.5%)
- [ ] Classifies severity: 5 CRITICAL, 1 HIGH, 6 MODERATE
- [ ] Displays accurate Z-scores (e.g., 2006 Q1 document Z=+10.97)
- [ ] Shows correct anomaly types (4 ballot, 8 document, 0 attendance)
- [ ] Direction indicators accurate (11 HIGH, 1 LOW)

### Anomaly Detection Logic
- [ ] |Z| < 1.5 = LOW severity 🟢
- [ ] 1.5 ≤ |Z| < 2.0 = MODERATE severity 🟡
- [ ] 2.0 ≤ |Z| < 2.5 = HIGH severity 🟠
- [ ] |Z| ≥ 2.5 = CRITICAL severity 🔴
- [ ] NO_ANOMALY when all |Z| < 1.5

### Visualizations
- [ ] Timeline scatter plot shows anomalies as colored points (severity-coded)
- [ ] Z-score distribution overlays normal curve with outliers highlighted
- [ ] Doughnut chart shows 33.3% ballot vs. 66.7% document split
- [ ] Heat map color scale: green → yellow → orange → red
- [ ] Bar chart shows Q2 has most anomalies (5 detected)
- [ ] Recent feed lists anomalies with full details

### Alert System
- [ ] Alert banner shows for CRITICAL anomalies in last 2 quarters
- [ ] Dismiss button hides banner and stores dismissal (24h)
- [ ] Alert message formatted: "{Year} {Quarter} {Type}: {Z-score} Z-score, {Direction}"
- [ ] Alert icon and colors match severity (🔴 red for CRITICAL)

### Performance
- [ ] Dashboard loads in < 3 seconds
- [ ] Chart rendering completes in < 1 second
- [ ] Smooth filter interactions
- [ ] Heat map renders 92 cells without lag

### Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works
- [ ] Screen reader announces anomaly alerts
- [ ] ARIA labels on all interactive elements
- [ ] Color contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (text), ≥ 3:1 (charts)
- [ ] Severity not conveyed by color alone (icons + text + labels)

### Responsive Design
- [ ] Mobile (320px-767px): Vertical layout, heat map scrollable, feed stacks
- [ ] Tablet (768px-1023px): 2-column grid
- [ ] Desktop (1024px+): 3-column grid, wide charts span 2 columns

### Multi-Language
- [ ] All 14 language files updated
- [ ] Alert banner messages localized
- [ ] Severity labels translated (Critical/Kritisk/Critique/etc.)
- [ ] Anomaly types and directions localized
- [ ] RTL support for Arabic and Hebrew

### Quality Gates
- [ ] HTML validation passes (HTMLHint)
- [ ] No broken links (linkinator)
- [ ] D3.js/Chart.js CDN with SRI hashes
- [ ] Security headers validated
- [ ] Alert system XSS-safe (sanitized messages)

