**Title:** Sanitize error messages to prevent information leakage

**Description:**
Some error messages may leak information about the internal state of the application or cryptographic operations, which could help attackers. Error messages should be informative for legitimate users but not reveal sensitive details.

**Security Impact:**
- Low severity
- Information leakage via verbose error messages
- Could aid attacker reconnaissance
- Best practice security enhancement

**Solution:**
Implement structured error handling with generic user-facing messages.

**Implementation Steps:**

1. Create error types in `src/errors.rs`:
```rust
use std::fmt;

#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum SecurityError {
    AuthenticationFailed,
    InvalidInput(String),
    StorageError,
    CryptographicError,
    PermissionDenied,
    RateLimitExceeded,
}

impl SecurityError {
    /// Returns user-friendly message that doesn't leak internal details
    pub fn user_message(&self) -> String {
        match self {
            Self::AuthenticationFailed => {
                "Incorrect master password. Please try again.".into()
            }
            Self::InvalidInput(field) => {
                format!("Invalid {}", field)
            }
            Self::StorageError => {
                "Unable to access password storage. Check file permissions.".into()
            }
            Self::CryptographicError => {
                "Encryption error occurred. Data may be corrupted.".into()
            }
            Self::PermissionDenied => {
                "Permission denied. Check file permissions.".into()
            }
            Self::RateLimitExceeded => {
                "Too many attempts. Please try again later.".into()
            }
        }
    }

    /// Returns detailed message for logging (not shown to user)
    pub fn debug_message(&self) -> String {
        format!("{:?}", self)
    }
}
```

2. Update `src/storage.rs` to use structured errors:
```rust
pub fn load_entries(&self, master_password: &str) -> Result<Vec<PasswordEntry>, SecurityError> {
    // ... existing code ...

    // Instead of:
    // .map_err(|e| format!("Decryption failed: {}", e))?;

    // Use:
    .map_err(|_| SecurityError::AuthenticationFailed)?;
}
```

3. Update UI handlers to use generic messages:
```rust
match storage.load_entries(&master_password) {
    Ok(entries) => { /* ... */ }
    Err(e) => {
        // Show generic message to user
        ui.set_status_message(e.user_message().into());

        // Log detailed error for debugging
        log::error!("Load failed: {}", e.debug_message());
    }
}
```

4. Add logging for detailed errors (for developers/debugging):
   - Log full error details with context
   - Include timestamps and operation details
   - Never show detailed crypto errors to users

**Files to Create:**
- `src/errors.rs` - Structured error types

**Files to Modify:**
- `src/lib.rs` - Add errors module
- `src/storage.rs` - Use SecurityError types
- `src/main.rs` - Handle errors with generic messages
- `tests/` - Update tests for new error types

**Testing:**
- Verify user messages are generic
- Verify detailed errors are logged
- Test all error paths
- Ensure no sensitive info in user messages

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Structured error types implemented
- [ ] User-facing messages are generic and safe
- [ ] Detailed errors logged for debugging
- [ ] No cryptographic details in user messages
- [ ] All error paths tested
- [ ] Documentation updated

**Priority:** 🔵 LOW
**Estimated Effort:** 2-3 hours
**Labels:** security, enhancement, code-quality

## Bug Description

`PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>` is a **static global singleton** that stores the "current" preprocessing pipeline. When multiple `AiModelBuilder` instances build models concurrently (e.g., in AutoML, hyperparameter search, or parallel training scenarios), they overwrite each other's pipeline configuration.

## Root Cause

### The static registry (`src/Preprocessing/PreprocessingRegistry.cs`)

```csharp
// Line 31: Global static class — one instance per type combination across entire AppDomain
public static class PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>
{
    // Line 33: Single global pipeline reference
    private static IDataTransformer<T, TInput, TInput>? _current;
    private static readonly object _lock = new();

    // Lines 48-64: Thread-safe get/set — but individual operations being thread-safe
    // doesn't prevent the TOCTOU race condition between Set and Use
    public static IDataTransformer<T, TInput, TInput>? Current { get; set; }
}
```

### Set in three places in `AiModelBuilder.cs`

Every `ConfigurePreprocessing()` overload sets the global registry:

```csharp
// Line 391 (Action<> overload):
PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>.Current = _preprocessingPipeline;

// Line 435 (single transformer overload):
PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>.Current = _preprocessingPipeline;

// Line 480 (pre-built pipeline overload):
PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>.Current = _preprocessingPipeline;
```

### Read during inference by `DocumentNeuralNetworkBase` (`src/Document/DocumentNeuralNetworkBase.cs`)

```csharp
// Lines 170-173: Neural network models read the global registry during inference
protected Tensor<T> PreprocessDocument(Tensor<T> rawImage)
{
    if (PreprocessingRegistry<T, Tensor<T>>.IsConfigured)  // Line 170
    {
        return PreprocessingRegistry<T, Tensor<T>>.Transform(rawImage);  // Line 172
    }
    return ApplyDefaultPreprocessing(rawImage);
}
```

## Race Condition Example

```csharp
// Thread 1: Building a regression model with StandardScaler
var builder1 = new AiModelBuilder<double, Matrix<double>, Vector<double>>()
    .ConfigurePreprocessing(new StandardScaler<double>())  // Sets global registry
    .ConfigureModel(new RidgeRegression<double>());

// Thread 2: Building a classification model with MinMaxScaler
var builder2 = new AiModelBuilder<double, Matrix<double>, Vector<double>>()
    .ConfigurePreprocessing(new MinMaxScaler<double>())  // OVERWRITES global registry!
    .ConfigureModel(new LogisticRegression<double>());

// Now Thread 1's pipeline was overwritten by Thread 2
// Thread 1 builds with MinMaxScaler instead of StandardScaler
await Task.WhenAll(builder1.BuildAsync(), builder2.BuildAsync());
```

## Impact

- **Concurrent model building** produces incorrect models (wrong preprocessing applied)
- **AutoML** workflows that build multiple models in parallel are affected
- **`DocumentNeuralNetworkBase`** models may use a preprocessing pipeline from a completely different model builder
- The `_lock` on individual get/set operations does NOT prevent the overwrite race — it only prevents torn reads

## Proposed Fix

Replace the static registry with instance-based preprocessing that flows through the builder:

```csharp
// REMOVE: PreprocessingRegistry static class entirely

// CHANGE: AiModelBuilder stores pipeline as instance field (already does this)
// CHANGE: Pass pipeline directly to models that need it, not via global state
// CHANGE: DocumentNeuralNetworkBase should receive pipeline via constructor/method, not global

// For ConfigurePreprocessing(), just set the instance field:
public IAiModelBuilder<T, TInput, TOutput> ConfigurePreprocessing(...)
{
    _preprocessingPipeline = pipeline;
    // REMOVE: PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>.Current = _preprocessingPipeline;
    return this;
}
```

For `DocumentNeuralNetworkBase.PreprocessDocument()`, pass the pipeline explicitly:
```csharp
// Option A: Constructor injection
public DocumentNeuralNetworkBase(IDataTransformer<T, Tensor<T>, Tensor<T>>? preprocessing = null)

// Option B: Method parameter
protected Tensor<T> PreprocessDocument(Tensor<T> rawImage, IDataTransformer<T, Tensor<T>, Tensor<T>>? pipeline = null)
```

## Files to Modify

| File | Line(s) | Change |
|------|---------|--------|
| `src/Preprocessing/PreprocessingRegistry.cs` | All | Remove entire class (or deprecate) |
| `src/AiModelBuilder.cs` | 391, 435, 480 | Remove `PreprocessingRegistry<T, TInput>.Current = ...` lines |
| `src/Document/DocumentNeuralNetworkBase.cs` | 170-173 | Replace `PreprocessingRegistry` usage with instance-based pipeline |

## Severity

**Medium** — Only affects concurrent/parallel model building. Single-threaded usage is fine. But AutoML and hyperparameter search are increasingly common use cases.

Related: #927

## Context
Child issue of #956 (Epic: Model Metadata Attributes & Source Generator Infrastructure)

Depends on: #957 (attributes), #958 (models annotated)

## Task
Create a Roslyn incremental source generator that auto-generates a static `ModelMetadataRegistry` class containing all model metadata collected from attributes at compile time.

### Generated Output

The generator should produce a class like:

```csharp
// <auto-generated/>
namespace AiDotNet.Generated;

public sealed class ModelMetadataEntry
{
    public Type ModelType { get; init; }
    public ModelDomain[] Domains { get; init; }
    public ModelCategory Category { get; init; }
    public ModelTask[] Tasks { get; init; }
    public ModelComplexity Complexity { get; init; }
    public Type InputType { get; init; }
    public Type OutputType { get; init; }
    public string? PaperName { get; init; }
    public string? PaperUrl { get; init; }
    public string Summary { get; init; }        // from XML <summary>
    public string BeginnerGuide { get; init; }   // from XML <remarks> For Beginners section
}

public static class ModelMetadataRegistry
{
    public static IReadOnlyList<ModelMetadataEntry> All { get; } = new ModelMetadataEntry[]
    {
        // ... one entry per model, auto-generated from attributes
    };

    // Query helpers
    public static IReadOnlyList<ModelMetadataEntry> GetByDomain(ModelDomain domain) => ...;
    public static IReadOnlyList<ModelMetadataEntry> GetByCategory(ModelCategory category) => ...;
    public static IReadOnlyList<ModelMetadataEntry> GetByTask(ModelTask task) => ...;
    public static IReadOnlyList<ModelMetadataEntry> GetByComplexity(ModelComplexity complexity) => ...;
    public static ModelMetadataEntry? GetByType(Type modelType) => ...;
}
```

### Key Requirements
- Zero runtime reflection - all metadata is statically emitted at compile time
- Query methods use pre-built lookup dictionaries (also generated)
- Include model count as a generated constant for quick stats
- Summary and BeginnerGuide text extracted from XML doc comments via Roslyn
- Use `IIncrementalGenerator` for incremental compilation performance

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Registry contains an entry for every attributed model class
- [ ] All 6 attribute values are correctly read and emitted
- [ ] Query methods work correctly for all domains, categories, tasks, and complexity levels
- [ ] No runtime reflection is used
- [ ] Generated code compiles on both net10.0 and net471
- [ ] Unit tests verify registry contents match expected model count

