Part of #956 — Model Domain Attributes

## Overview
Create a Roslyn incremental source generator that produces a strongly-typed, IntelliSense-friendly discovery API from `[ModelDomain]`, `[ModelCategory]`, and `[ModelTask]` attributes on model classes.

## Generated API Shape

```csharp
// Auto-generated static class
public static partial class Models
{
    public static class Vision
    {
        public static class Classification
        {
            public static Type ResNet => typeof(ResNet<>);
            public static Type EfficientNet => typeof(EfficientNet<>);
            public static Type VGG => typeof(VGG<>);
            // ... all Vision+Classification models
        }
        public static class Detection { /* ... */ }
        public static class Segmentation { /* ... */ }
        public static class SuperResolution { /* ... */ }
    }
    public static class Audio
    {
        public static class SpeechRecognition { /* ... */ }
        public static class SourceSeparation { /* ... */ }
    }
    public static class Language { /* ... */ }
    // ... all 17 domains × relevant tasks
}
```

## Generator Requirements

### Input
- Scan all classes decorated with `[ModelDomain(...)]`, `[ModelCategory(...)]`, and `[ModelTask(...)]`
- Group by Domain → Task hierarchy

### Output
- `Models.g.cs` — static partial class with nested classes per domain/task
- Each leaf property returns `Type` of the model class
- XML doc comments on each property with model name, complexity, and paper reference (if `[ModelPaper]` present)

### Design Decisions
- **Flat properties** (not methods) for simplest IntelliSense experience
- **Open generic types** (`typeof(ResNet<>)`) since `T` isn't known at discovery time
- Models with **multiple domains** appear in each domain's subtree
- Models with **multiple tasks** appear in each task's subtree
- **Empty subtrees** are omitted (no `Models.Robotics.Translation` if no models match)

### Additional Query Methods

```csharp
public static partial class Models
{
    // Get all models for a domain
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetByDomain(ModelDomain domain);

    // Get all models for a task
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetByTask(ModelTask task);

    // Get all models matching domain + task
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetByDomainAndTask(ModelDomain domain, ModelTask task);

    // Get all models by complexity
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetByComplexity(ModelComplexity complexity);

    // Get all models by category
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetByCategory(ModelCategory category);
}
```

## Implementation Notes

- Use `IIncrementalGenerator` (not `ISourceGenerator`) for performance
- Register syntax provider filtering for `[ModelDomain]` attribute
- Collect all matching types, group, and emit nested static classes
- Must handle models with multiple attribute instances (multi-domain, multi-task)
- net471 compatible output (no C# 10+ features in generated code)

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Generator produces `Models.g.cs` with domain/task hierarchy
- [ ] IntelliSense shows model types when typing `Models.Vision.`
- [ ] Query methods return correct model types for each enum value
- [ ] Models with multiple domains/tasks appear in all relevant subtrees
- [ ] Empty subtrees are omitted
- [ ] XML doc comments include model metadata
- [ ] Builds on both net10.0 and net471

## Dependencies
- #957 (attributes and enums must exist first)
- #958 (models must be annotated for generator to have input)

## Parent Epic
Part of #956 — Model Domain Attributes

## Overview
Create a Roslyn incremental source generator that analyzes generic constraints, interface implementations, and attribute metadata to produce a compile-time compatibility matrix showing which models work with which optimizers, loss functions, and preprocessors.

## Problem Statement
Currently, users discover incompatibilities at runtime when they pair a model with an incompatible optimizer or loss function. This generator shifts that discovery to compile time by analyzing type constraints and producing a queryable compatibility matrix.

## Generator Requirements

### Input Sources
1. **Generic constraints** — e.g., `where T : IFloatingPoint<T>` limits which numeric types work
2. **Interface implementations** — e.g., `ISupportsRegularization<T>` indicates optimizer compatibility
3. **`[ModelCategory]` attribute** — classifiers need classification loss functions, regressors need regression losses
4. **`[ModelTask]` attribute** — certain tasks imply certain preprocessors
5. **Constructor parameters** — required dependencies reveal what components a model needs

### Output: `ModelCompatibility.g.cs`

```csharp
// Auto-generated
public static partial class ModelCompatibility
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Returns optimizers compatible with the given model type.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetCompatibleOptimizers(Type modelType);

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns loss functions compatible with the given model type.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetCompatibleLossFunctions(Type modelType);

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns preprocessors recommended for the given model type.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetRecommendedPreprocessors(Type modelType);

    /// <summary>
    /// Checks if a model and optimizer are compatible.
    /// </summary>
    public static bool IsCompatible(Type modelType, Type optimizerType);

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns all compatibility information for a model.
    /// </summary>
    public static ModelCompatibilityInfo GetInfo(Type modelType);
}

public class ModelCompatibilityInfo
{
    public Type ModelType { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<Type> CompatibleOptimizers { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<Type> CompatibleLossFunctions { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<Type> RecommendedPreprocessors { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Warnings { get; }
}
```

### Compatibility Rules

| Model Category | Compatible Loss Functions | Compatible Optimizers |
|---|---|---|
| Classifier | CrossEntropy, BinaryCrossEntropy, Hinge, FocalLoss | All gradient-based |
| Regression | MSE, MAE, Huber, LogCosh | All gradient-based |
| GAN | Adversarial, Wasserstein, HingeLoss | Adam, RMSProp (not SGD recommended) |
| Autoencoder | MSE, BCE, KLDivergence | All gradient-based |
| TimeSeries | MSE, MAE, QuantileLoss | Adam, AdaGrad |
| SurvivalModel | CoxPartialLikelihood, LogRankLoss | Adam, L-BFGS |

### Diagnostic Warnings

The generator should also emit warnings (not errors) for suspicious combinations:
- `AIDNT001`: Model uses `[ModelCategory(Classifier)]` but paired with regression loss function
- `AIDNT002`: Model uses `[ModelCategory(GAN)]` but optimizer is plain SGD
- `AIDNT003`: Model requires specific preprocessor but none detected in pipeline

## Implementation Notes

- Use `IIncrementalGenerator` for performance
- Analyze `SyntaxTree` and `SemanticModel` for generic constraints and interfaces
- Cross-reference with attribute data from `[ModelCategory]` and `[ModelTask]`
- Build lookup dictionaries at compile time, emit as static readonly collections
- net471 compatible output

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Generator produces `ModelCompatibility.g.cs`
- [ ] `GetCompatibleOptimizers()` returns correct types based on model category
- [ ] `GetCompatibleLossFunctions()` returns correct types based on model category
- [ ] `IsCompatible()` correctly validates model+optimizer pairs
- [ ] Diagnostic warnings emitted for suspicious combinations
- [ ] Builds on both net10.0 and net471

## Dependencies
- #957 (attributes and enums must exist first)
- #958 (models must be annotated)
- #960 (registry generator provides model metadata at compile time)

## Parent Epic
Part of #956 — Model Domain Attributes

## Overview
Create a Roslyn incremental source generator that cross-references model classes (decorated with `[ModelDomain]`) against test classes to identify untested models. Optionally generates skeleton test files for models that lack test coverage.

## Problem Statement
With ~700 model classes, it is easy for new models to be added without corresponding tests. This generator provides:
1. **Compile-time warnings** for any model class without a matching test class
2. **Optional skeleton test generation** to jumpstart test writing

## Generator Requirements

### Input
1. **Model classes** — all classes with `[ModelDomain(...)]` attribute
2. **Test classes** — classes in the test project with `[Fact]` or `[Theory]` attributes, or classes whose name matches `{ModelName}Tests`
3. **Convention matching** — `ResNet<T>` matches `ResNetTests`, `ResNet_Tests`, or any test class containing a test method referencing `ResNet`

### Output 1: Diagnostics

```
// Compile-time warnings
warning AIDNT010: Model 'WaveGrad<T>' (Audio/Generation) has no corresponding test class.
warning AIDNT010: Model 'DiffusionTransformer<T>' (Vision/Generation) has no corresponding test class.
// Info-level for models with tests
info AIDNT011: 642 of 700 models have test coverage (91.7%).
```

### Output 2: Test Coverage Report (`TestCoverage.g.cs`)

```csharp
// Auto-generated
public static partial class TestCoverage
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Models that have corresponding test classes.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> TestedModels { get; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Models that do NOT have corresponding test classes.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> UntestedModels { get; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Coverage percentage (0-100).
    /// </summary>
    public static double CoveragePercent { get; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Get untested models by domain.
    /// </summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<Type> GetUntestedByDomain(ModelDomain domain);
}
```

### Output 3: Optional Skeleton Tests

When enabled via MSBuild property `<GenerateTestSkeletons>true</GenerateTestSkeletons>`, generates skeleton test files:

```csharp
// Auto-generated: WaveGradTests.g.cs
using Xunit;

namespace AiDotNet.Tests.Audio;

/// <summary>
/// Auto-generated test skeleton for WaveGrad.
/// Domain: Audio | Category: NeuralNetwork | Task: Generation
/// TODO: Implement actual test logic.
/// </summary>
public class WaveGradTests
{
    [Fact]
    public void Constructor_CreatesInstance()
    {
        // Arrange & Act
        // var model = new WaveGrad<double>(...);

        // Assert
        // Assert.NotNull(model);
        throw new NotImplementedException("TODO: Implement test for WaveGrad");
    }

    [Fact]
    public void Forward_ProducesFiniteOutput()
    {
        // Arrange
        // var model = new WaveGrad<double>(...);
        // var input = ...; // TODO: Create appropriate test input

        // Act
        // var output = model.Forward(input);

        // Assert
        // Assert.All output values are finite
        throw new NotImplementedException("TODO: Implement forward pass test for WaveGrad");
    }
}
```

### Test Matching Heuristics

The generator uses these rules to match models to tests (in priority order):
1. **Exact name match**: `ResNet<T>` → `ResNetTests` class exists
2. **Partial name match**: `ResNet<T>` → any test class containing `ResNet` in its name
3. **Method reference**: Any test method that references `new ResNet<` or `typeof(ResNet<`
4. **Attribute reference**: `[InlineData(typeof(ResNet<double>))]` in any theory

### Configuration via MSBuild

```xml
<PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Enable/disable test skeleton generation (default: false) -->
    <GenerateTestSkeletons>false</GenerateTestSkeletons>

    <!-- Severity for untested model warnings (default: Warning) -->
    <UntestedModelSeverity>Warning</UntestedModelSeverity>

    <!-- Minimum coverage threshold before error (default: 0, disabled) -->
    <MinTestCoveragePercent>80</MinTestCoveragePercent>
</PropertyGroup>
```

## Implementation Notes

- Use `IIncrementalGenerator` for performance
- Requires cross-project analysis: model project + test project
- The generator runs in the **test project** (where it has visibility into both model types via references and test types via the current compilation)
- Use `AdditionalTextsProvider` or assembly attribute scanning for cross-project data if needed
- net471 compatible output

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Generator emits `AIDNT010` warning for each model without a test class
- [ ] Generator emits `AIDNT011` info with coverage summary
- [ ] `TestCoverage.g.cs` is generated with correct tested/untested lists
- [ ] Optional skeleton test generation works when `GenerateTestSkeletons=true`
- [ ] Test matching heuristics correctly identify tested models
- [ ] Coverage percentage is accurate
- [ ] Builds on both net10.0 and net471

## Dependencies
- #957 (attributes and enums must exist first)
- #958 (models must be annotated for generator to discover them)

