    public IReadOnlyList<Type> CompatibleOptimizers { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<Type> CompatibleLossFunctions { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<Type> RecommendedPreprocessors { get; }
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Warnings { get; }
}
```

### Compatibility Rules

| Model Category | Compatible Loss Functions | Compatible Optimizers |
|---|---|---|
| Classifier | CrossEntropy, BinaryCrossEntropy, Hinge, FocalLoss | All gradient-based |
| Regression | MSE, MAE, Huber, LogCosh | All gradient-based |
| GAN | Adversarial, Wasserstein, HingeLoss | Adam, RMSProp (not SGD recommended) |
| Autoencoder | MSE, BCE, KLDivergence | All gradient-based |
| TimeSeries | MSE, MAE, QuantileLoss | Adam, AdaGrad |
| SurvivalModel | CoxPartialLikelihood, LogRankLoss | Adam, L-BFGS |

### Diagnostic Warnings

The generator should also emit warnings (not errors) for suspicious combinations:
- `AIDNT001`: Model uses `[ModelCategory(Classifier)]` but paired with regression loss function
- `AIDNT002`: Model uses `[ModelCategory(GAN)]` but optimizer is plain SGD
- `AIDNT003`: Model requires specific preprocessor but none detected in pipeline

