### Problem
Checkpointing is essential for long-running Spark applications to truncate lineage and improve fault tolerance. The JS client needs `checkpoint()` and `localCheckpoint()` support as defined in the Spark Connect protocol.

### Implementation Guidance

**1. API Design**
```typescript
class DataFrame {
  // Reliable checkpoint (persists to HDFS/S3)
  async checkpoint(eager?: boolean): Promise<DataFrame>;

  // Local checkpoint (persists locally, less reliable)
  async localCheckpoint(eager?: boolean): Promise<DataFrame>;
}
```

**2. Proto Mapping**
- Reference `commands.proto`: CheckpointCommand (line 51)
- Create command with local vs reliable flag
- Handle eager execution option

**3. Implementation Example**
```typescript
async checkpoint(eager:  boolean = true): Promise<DataFrame> {
  const checkpointCmd = {
    relation: this.plan.relation,
    local: false,
    eager: eager
  };

  const plan = this.spark.planFromCommandBuilder(b => 
    b.withCheckpointCommand(checkpointCmd)
  );

  await this.spark.client.execute(plan. plan);
  return this;
}

async localCheckpoint(eager:  boolean = true): Promise<DataFrame> {
  const checkpointCmd = {
    relation: this. plan.relation,
    local: true,
    eager: eager
  };

  const plan = this.spark.planFromCommandBuilder(b => 
    b.withCheckpointCommand(checkpointCmd)
  );

  await this.spark. client.execute(plan.plan);
  return this;
}
```

**4. Usage Example**
```typescript
// Create a complex DataFrame
let df = spark.range(1, 1000000);
df = df.filter("id % 2 = 0");
df = df.groupBy("id").count();

// Checkpoint to truncate lineage
df = await df.checkpoint();

// Continue with more transformations
df = df.filter("count > 10");
```

### Configuration
- Users must set `spark.sql.checkpoint.location` config
- Default checkpoint directory configuration
- Storage level for checkpointed data

### References
- Spark proto: `commands.proto` (CheckpointCommand)
- [Spark Checkpoint Documentation](https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/rdd-programming-guide.html#checkpointing)
- [Go implementation reference](https://github.com/apache/spark-connect-go/tree/main/spark/sql)

### Testing Requirements
- Test both checkpoint and localCheckpoint
- Test eager vs lazy checkpointing
- Verify lineage truncation
- Test with various storage configurations

---
- **Labels:** enhancement, fault-tolerance

